From 0180b861ffa1851b9489341ec5d9d014ed27d28a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:43:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Translate Fusion 360 Y-up coordinates to SolidCraft Z-up
 by default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fusion 360 uses a Y-up right-handed coordinate system by default,
whereas SolidCraft uses a standard Z-up right-handed coordinate system.
This causes Fusion 360 models imported into SolidCraft to appear lying on
their side.

Orient root occurrences for Fusion 360 designs (+90° about +X:
X -> X, Y -> Z, Z -> -Y) by default, while providing --stand-up and
--no-stand-up CLI flags for user override.
